            <h3>Terminals at Denver International Airport</h3>
            <p>Denver operates a single main terminal (Jeppesen Terminal) with three concourses (A, B, C) connected by an efficient underground train system.</p>
            <h4>Jeppesen Terminal</h4>
            <p>The central check-in and baggage claim facility serving all airlines.</p>
            <b>Facilities:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>International and domestic check-in counters</li>
                <li>Security screening with TSA PreCheck and CLEAR lanes</li>
                <li>Ground transportation center with rental cars, taxis, and transit</li>
                <li>Hotel and parking reservations desk</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Concourse A</h4>
            <p>Serves international carriers and some domestic operators. United's international flights and foreign airlines like Lufthansa and British Airways operate from here.</p>
            <b>Features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>International gates with customs and immigration facilities</li>
                <li>United Club and international airline lounges</li>
                <li>Duty-free shopping for departing international passengers</li>
                <li>Diverse dining from fast casual to sit-down restaurants</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Concourse B</h4>
            <p>United Airlines' primary domestic hub concourse with extensive gate capacity.</p>
            <b>Features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Numerous United Club locations</li>
                <li>Wide selection of retail and food options</li>
                <li>Comfortable passenger waiting areas with charging stations</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Concourse C</h4>
            <p>Primarily serves Southwest Airlines and other domestic carriers.</p>
            <b>Features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Local and national dining options</li>
                <li>Retail stores and newsstands</li>
                <li>Passenger service amenities</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Transportation to Denver International Airport</h3>
            <h4>A-Line Commuter Rail</h4>
            <p>The Regional Transportation District's A-Line provides direct rail service between Denver Union Station and the airport.</p>
            <b>Benefits:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Most affordable option at approximately $10.50</li>
                <li>Reliable 37-minute journey with departures every 15-30 minutes</li>
                <li>Avoids highway traffic entirely</li>
                <li>Connects to downtown hotels, light rail, and Amtrak</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Taxi and Rideshare</h4>
            <p>Uber, Lyft, and traditional taxis offer door-to-door service.</p>
            <b>Travel times:</b>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Off-peak:</b> 30-40 minutes</li>
                <li><b>Rush hour:</b> 45-70 minutes</li>
                <li><b>Cost:</b> $35-$60 depending on destination and demand</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Airport Shuttle</h4>
            <p>Numerous private shuttle companies serve Denver metro area hotels and residences with scheduled and on-demand service.</p>
            <h4>Driving and Parking</h4>
            <p>Denver International offers extensive parking options:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Short-Term:</b> Premium rates for brief visits and passenger pickup</li>
                <li><b>Long-Term:</b> Economical covered and uncovered options with shuttle service</li>
                <li><b>Reserved:</b> Guaranteed spaces during peak periods</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Lounges at Denver International Airport</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>United Club (Concourse A and B) -</b> Multiple locations for MileagePlus
                    elites and eligible cardholders
                </li>
                <li><b>Delta Sky Club (Concourse A) - </b>For Sky Club members and eligible passengers</li>
                <li><b>American Express Centurion Lounge (Concourse C) -</b> Premium lounge for Platinum and Centurion cardholders</li>
                <li><b>USO Lounge -</b> For active military personnel and families</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Amenities typically include: Comfortable seating, complimentary food and beverages, Wi-Fi, charging stations, shower facilities, and business centers.
                <h3>Arrival Airport: Paris Charles de Gaulle Airport (CDG)</h3>
            <p>Charles de Gaulle stands as France's principal aviation gateway and one of Europe's most important hub airports. Its complex layout reflects decades of expansion, with multiple terminals handling distinct traffic flows.</p>
