            <h3>Charles de Gaulle Terminals</h3>
            <p>CDG operates three main terminal complexes, each with sub-terminals that can confuse first-time visitors.</p>
            <h4>Terminal 1</h4>
            <p>The iconic circular terminal designed by Paul Andreu, handling primarily Star Alliance carriers and some non-alliance airlines.</p>
            <b>Facilities:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>International check-in and arrivals</li>
                <li>Baggage claim and lost luggage services</li>
                <li>Duty-free shopping and dining</li>
                <li>Connected to other terminals via CDGVAL automated shuttle</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Terminal 2</h4>
            <p>The largest and most complex terminal, subdivided into halls 2A through 2G. Air France and SkyTeam partners dominate here.</p>
            <b>Facilities:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Air France check-in and lounges across multiple halls</li>
                <li>Extensive duty-free and luxury retail in 2E/2F</li>
                <li>RER B and TGV train stations accessible from 2C-2F</li>
                <li>Multiple airline lounges including Air France's premium offerings</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Terminal 3</h4>
            <p>Dedicated primarily to low-cost and charter carriers.</p>
            <b>Features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Simplified check-in and boarding processes</li>
                <li>Basic passenger amenities</li>
                <li>CDGVAL connection to Terminals 1 and 2</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Immigration and Customs at Charles de Gaulle</h3>
            <p>Passengers arriving from Denver proceed through Schengen entry formalities.</p>
            <b>Requirements:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Valid passport with minimum three months' validity beyond intended departure</li>
                <li>ETIAS authorization (once implemented) or visa if required</li>
                <li>Proof of accommodation for border inspection</li>
                <li>Return or onward travel documentation</li>
                <li>Travel insurance documentation (recommended but not mandatory)</li>
            </ul>
            US citizens enjoy visa-free access for tourism stays up to 90 days within any 180-day Schengen period.
            <h3>Transportation from Charles de Gaulle to Central Paris</h3>
            <h4>RER B Commuter Train</h4>
            <p>The most economical option connecting CDG to central Paris stations including Gare du Nord, Châtelet-Les Halles, and Saint-Michel Notre-Dame.</p>
            <b>Benefits:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Cost: approximately €11.80</li>
                <li>Journey time: 35-45 minutes to central Paris</li>
                <li>Frequent departures every 10-15 minutes</li>
                <li>Direct access to major Metro interchange stations</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>RoissyBus</h4>
            <p>Dedicated express bus service from CDG Terminals 1, 2, and 3 to Opéra in central Paris.</p>
            <b>Features:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Cost approximately €16.20</li>
                <li>Journey time: 60-75 minutes depending on traffic</li>
                <li>Departures every 15-20 minutes</li>
                <li>Drops near major department stores and Metro connections</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Taxi</h4>
            <p>Official Parisian taxis operate from designated ranks outside each terminal.</p>
            <b>Typical fares:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>To central Paris: €55-€62 flat rate (right bank) or €50-€58 (left bank)</li>
                <li>Night supplement applies between 7 PM and 7 AM</li>
                <li>Always use official taxis from marked ranks; avoid solicitors in arrivals hall</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Private Transfer and Rideshare</h4>
            <p>Pre-booked private cars, Uber, and Bolt operate from CDG with variable pricing based on demand and vehicle class.</p>
            <h4>Car Hire</h4>
            <p>Major rental agencies maintain desks at CDG for travelers planning road trips to Normandy, the Loire Valley, or the Champagne region.</p>
